# ============================================================================
# .gitignore for the SECOND repository (root = pf_bridge\)
# deny-all + allowlist, per chief verdict 2026-08-20 condition (1)
# Panya decisions 2026-08-20 ~12:1x: VITAL_REGISTRY = IN, evidence_screens = IN
# ============================================================================
# Rule of this file: line 1 denies everything; every `!` below re-opens one
# thing by name; git does NOT descend into an excluded directory, so each
# directory is opened before its contents. Last matching line wins, so the
# hard-deny block at the bottom is the final word.

/*

# ---- root: docs, findings, factpacks, queue, continuation ----
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/*.md

# ---- root: our own derived data + tools (NOT byte copies of the binary) ----
!/CANON_SHA.txt
!/NEW_SESSION_OPENER.txt
!/IMAGE_ACCESS_COST.tsv
!/VITAL_REGISTRY_FROM_CLIENT_BINARY_20260817.tsv
!/FACTPACK_L2_CLASSCENSUS001_20260820.json
!/FACTPACK_L2_CLASSCENSUS001_20260820.tsv
!/DRAFT_gitignore_runtime_state.txt
!/DRAFT_gitignore_REPO2_20260820.txt

# ---- the cloud round lock (Panya order 2026-08-20 18:45) ----
# This one MUST be tracked, unlike every other lock in this project.  The two
# flag files guard one machine's ports, processes and index and must never
# travel; this file is the opposite - it is how two cloud rounds that cannot
# see each other take turns, and it works only because a push that is not a
# fast-forward is rejected atomically by the server.  A lock you win by writing
# a file is not a lock; a lock you win by pushing is.  Deliberately not named
# LOCK_* and deliberately not .txt, so the /LOCK_*.txt deny above cannot eat it.
!/cloud_round_lock.json
!/*.ps1
!/*.bat
!/*.py

# ---- directories that carry the project's memory ----
!/agent_kit/
!/agent_kit/**
!/notes_to_chief/
!/notes_to_chief/**
!/archive/
!/archive/**
!/templates/
!/templates/**
!/staged/
!/staged/**
!/drafts/
!/drafts/**
!/codex_orders/
!/codex_orders/**
!/image_queries/
!/image_queries/**
!/evidence_screens/
!/evidence_screens/**

# ---- patches/: chief-authored tool patches travelling cloud -> bridge ----
# (GT-047 job 0: the validator source came IN via a notes_to_chief letter;
# the patched file goes BACK via this folder so it travels with an exact
# sha256 instead of being re-pasted through a fenced code block.)
!/patches/
!/patches/**

# ---- factpack_L1: open the folder, keep ONLY the four safe members ----
!/factpack_L1/
/factpack_L1/*
!/factpack_L1/MANIFEST.md
!/factpack_L1/TIMING.md
!/factpack_L1/blocks_256.tsv
!/factpack_L1/make_factpack_l1.py

# ---- external/: the Codex RE deliverable (analytic tables: VA/span/sha
# rows - NOT byte extracts of the client binary).  Same pattern as
# factpack_L1: open the folder, deny everything inside, then allow ONLY
# members named here after a human at the bridge confirmed each one is a
# derived table.  strings_/pe_-style byte dumps must never be listed here;
# the hard-deny block below keeps the final word on binaries either way.
# All 8 delivered tables are now named: the first 5 were whitelisted by
# chief round R129, the last 3 by R131 after the bridge letter of
# 2026-08-23 20:39 named them and swept them clean (820 rows, no raw
# bytes).  Name-only entries, never a glob.
!/external/
/external/*
!/external/00_SEARCH_HERE_FIRST.md
!/external/PF_PROTOCOL_REGISTRY.tsv
!/external/PF_SERIALIZER_FIELDS.tsv
!/external/PF_RUNTIME_CLASSMAP.tsv
!/external/PF_INPUT_INVENTORY.tsv
!/external/PF_FIELD_VALIDATION.tsv
!/external/PF_PROTOCOL_PRIORITY.tsv
!/external/PF_DATA_EVIDENCE.tsv
!/external/PF_TAG_CENSUS.tsv

# ---- gamedata/: every table from the game's own data files, extracted by
# pf_extract_gamedata.py (188 tables / 2,365 columns from the 4 B_*.pc_
# files).  Panya ruled 2026-08-23 that derived material may go to the
# remote, and this repo is private.
#
# Why this block uses shapes and not one line per file, unlike external/:
# external/ mixes derived tables with extractor scripts that carry
# hardcoded byte guards, so every member there needs a human eye.  This
# folder holds nothing but one script's output.  Swept before opening it:
# columns whose size is not 1/2/4/8 (the only path that would emit
# raw.hex()) = 0, and long hex blobs across all 188 TSVs = 0.  Every value
# is an int, a float or a game string.  Anything that is not one of the
# shapes below stays ignored, so a stray file cannot ride along.
!/gamedata/
/gamedata/*
!/gamedata/00_SEARCH_HERE_FIRST.md
!/gamedata/PF_GAMEDATA_INDEX.tsv
!/gamedata/PF_GAMEDATA_COLUMNS.tsv
!/gamedata/pf_extract_gamedata.py
!/gamedata/_*_meta.json
!/gamedata/tables/
!/gamedata/tables/*.tsv

# ---- gamedata/lua/ + gamedata/scene/: the game's own scripts and native
# scene files, decoded by pf_decode_lua_npc.py on 2026-08-24 (616 Lua from
# .lu_ $pcz containers, 289 .npc scene files parsed to exact EOF).
# Swept before opening it, across all 616 .lua and all 289 .tsv:
#   absolute paths 0, UNC paths 0, emails 0, URLs 0, IPv4 0,
#   password/secret/token/licence words 0, hex blobs >=32 chars 0,
#   dofile/loadfile/require/io.open/os.execute call sites 0.
# pf_decode_lua_npc.py inspected separately (766 lines): no hardcoded byte
# guards, no long hex literals - only the "$pcz" magic and text regexes.
# Shapes are pinned the same way tables/ is: everything under lua/ and
# scene/ is re-ignored, then only directories plus *.lua / *.placements.tsv
# are re-opened, so a stray .bin, .dec, .bak or .log cannot ride along.
# Verified with git check-ignore on a mock tree before being written here.
!/gamedata/PF_GAMEDATA_LUA_INDEX.tsv
!/gamedata/PF_GAMEDATA_SCENE_INDEX.tsv
!/gamedata/pf_decode_lua_npc.py
!/gamedata/pf_lua_api_census.py
!/gamedata/PF_GAMEDATA_LUA_API.tsv
!/gamedata/PF_LUA_API_SPEC.md
!/gamedata/lua/
/gamedata/lua/**
!/gamedata/lua/**/
!/gamedata/lua/**/*.lua
!/gamedata/scene/
/gamedata/scene/**
!/gamedata/scene/**/
!/gamedata/scene/**/*.placements.tsv

# ---- workflows: merge a cloud round's pull request (chief round 110) ----
# Line 1 of this file is `/*`, so git does not even descend into .github/
# unless the directory is opened by name BEFORE its contents.  Both lines are
# needed; the first one alone opens an empty door.
!/.github/
!/.github/**

# ---- subagent definitions, so a cloud round has the same specialists a bridge
# round had.  Claude Code picks these up automatically from the cloned repo.
# Both lines are needed: line 1 of this file is `/*`, and git does not descend
# into a directory it has already excluded.
!/.claude/
!/.claude/**

# ---- one file per round, so two pull requests never touch one line ----
# prompt v4 sends each cloud round's log to rounds/R<NNN>_*.md instead of
# inserting at line 3 of CHIEF_CONTINUATION.md, which collided every time.
!/rounds/
!/rounds/**

# ---- runtime flags: whoever holds the machine owns these, never sync ----
/LOCK.txt
/LOCK_*.txt
/PANYA_PRESENT.txt
/bridge_loop_state.txt
/watchdog_last_check.txt

# ============================================================================
# HARD DENIES - last word. Nothing above may re-open these.
# ============================================================================
**/*.log
**/*.bin
**/*.bi_
**/*.dmp
**/*.exe
**/*.dll
**/*.pyd
**/*.zip
**/*.7z
**/*.rar
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.tgz
**/*.pcap
**/*.cap
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-wal
**/*.sqlite3-shm
**/*.db
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.bak_*
**/*.tmp
**/*.part

# images: denied everywhere, allowed only in the curated evidence folder
**/*.png
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.gif
**/*.mp4
!/evidence_screens/**

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER ON A REMOTE: byte-for-byte extracts of the third-party client binary.
# chief verdict condition (2). These stay on Panya's machine forever.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/factpack_L1/strings_*.tsv
/factpack_L1/pe_*.tsv
